                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Straight off the bat, LIMBO pushes you into the perspective of a scared little boy stuck in a dark, gloomy forest all alone. You're not told to do anything, just [i]feel[/i]. \n\nWhile there aren't any instructions, the environment makes it pretty clear what the mechanics are and how the game is intended to be. The story's also something you kind of realise as you go, rather than understand from some dialogues or other characters. My absolute favourite parts have gotta be the atmosphere, plot and tastefully-chosen colour palette (or otherwise lack of, one can say?) that all come together to create such an intense mood throughout this short yet impactful journey.\n\nLIMBO's a one-of-a-kind [b]work of art[/b]. \nWe so need this genre of games back.",
